# dist/ is shipped verbatim. install.cmd verifies every downloaded file's SHA256 against
# dist/manifest.txt, and tools/release.sh computes those hashes on the bytes in the working tree.
# Git must therefore never normalise line endings on check-in (core.autocrlf=true does, for any
# file it classifies as text): a CRLF SubModule.xml hashed on disk was stored and served as LF,
# and every install.cmd rejected the first v1.3.2 push (2026-09-04). tools/lint-scripts.sh fails
# if this attribute is missing for a manifest file.
dist/** -text
